-------------------------------------------------------

Modified by QMesh (2026) for the DSV4.1 AFD-TP3 experiment:

- p7/mhc_quant/overlay/models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/ops/mhc.py
  mHC fused MXFP8 quant: adds a prequant boundary path that runs
  `mhc_post_norm_quant` and carries the F8_128x4 activation as `_moet_qa`,
  with per-(n, hidden, device) q/sf buffers; falls back to `mhc_post_norm`.
- p7/mhc_quant/overlay/models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/model.py
  mHC fused MXFP8 quant: enables prequant at the attention boundary only; the
  FFN boundary and `write_kv` keep the default path.
- p7/mhc_quant/overlay/models/deepseek_v41/attention.py
  mHC fused MXFP8 quant: `_fused_wqa_wkv_gemm` consumes `_moet_qa` when the
  FlashInfer MXFP8 kernel declares the matching dynamic input; every other
  kernel uses the served path.
- p7/mhc_quant/kernel/mhc_post_norm_sm120.cu
- p7/mhc_quant/kernel/mhc_post_norm_sm120.py
  Derived from vLLM-Moet mHC sources; see "Derived mHC kernel" below.
- p7/dspark_retention/overlay/vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_planning.py
  DSpark retention: when `use_dspark()` is active, retain at least
  `num_speculative_tokens + 1` tokens below a sliding-window boundary; the
  non-DSpark path is unchanged.
- p7/dspark_retention/overlay/vllm/v1/attention/backends/mla/sparse_swa.py
  DSpark retention: map context positions in the null SWA block (block 0) to
  slot -1 so they cannot alias real KV; other paths are unchanged.

